'''Hugh Sion''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[New Republic pilot|pilot]] who flew for the [[New Republic Defense Fleet Starfighter Corps|New Republic Starfighter Corps]] in [[34 ABY]] during the [[Cold War]] between the militant [[First Order]] and the [[New Republic]]. During the conflict, he joined fellow [[pilot]] [[Mia Gabon]] under the command of [[Kazuda Xiono]] on a [[Mission to rendezvous with the Resistance|mission]] to rendezvous with [[Commander]] [[Poe Dameron]] of the [[Resistance]] to deliver intelligence. After coming under attack by [[Major]] [[Elrik Vonreg]] of the First Order, Sion and Gabon managed to escape into [[hyperspace]] back to base while Xiono stayed behind to see the mission through, eventually being rescued from Vonreg by Dameron himself.

Sion went on to join the Resistance during the [[First Order-Resistance War]], flying for [[Jade Squadron]] under Commander [[Venisa Doza]]. The [[squadron]] was allowed by Doza's husband, [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza]] of the [[supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]'', to use his tanker as the launching point for a [[Mission to Dantooine (Resistance)|mission]] to the [[planet]] [[Dantooine]] to rescue Resistance recruits from the [[Blockade of Dantooine|First Order-controlled]] world. Sion was reunited with Xiono on the tanker and introduced his friend to his new wingmate [[Norath Kev]]. Commander Doza briefed Sion and the rest of the squadron, including the newly added [[Hype Fazon]], [[Torra Doza]], and Xiono of [[Ace Squadron]], in the [[Aces' Lounge]] aboard the ''Colossus''.

The expanded squadron departed for Dantooine and was attacked by a [[scout]]ing party of [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter]]s, though Jade Squadron defeated the party and continued on their mission. While escorting the [[convoy]] of [[Resistance shuttle|transports]], the [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Thunderer]]'' arrived, and First Order forces, including former ''Colossus'' residents [[Tamara Ryvora]] and [[Jace Rucklin]], attacked Sion and the convoy. Ryvora managed to trail Xiono, but Sion damaged her fighter, and the two surviving shuttles&mdash;[[Shuttle two (Resistance)|one]] having been destroyed&mdash;and Jade Squadron escaped back to the ''Colossus''.

The ''Colossus'' traveled to the [[Barabesh system]] while evading the First Order, and Xiono and the [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Jarek Yeager]] attempted to [[Battle of Barabesh|rescue]] Ryvora, as she had secretly expressed a desire to desert from the First Order. The trio was captured by First Order [[Agent]] [[Tierny]] and Commander [[Pyre]] and brought aboard the ''Thunderer'', which traveled to the Barabesh system to destroy the ''Colossus''. Captain Doza gathered the tanker's denizens, including Sion, and begged them to fight the First Order, and a [[hologram]] of Xiono and Ryvora moved them to action. Jade Squadron joined forces with Ace Squadron and launched from the ''Colossus'' under Commander Doza, and the combined forces targeted the ''Thunderer''{{'s}} [[engine]]s. After several ineffective runs, the [[Star Destroyer]]'s [[Deflector shield|shields]] were disabled by the [[astromech droid]] [[CB-23]], allowing the fighters to destroy the ''Thunderer'' as Xiono, Yeager, Ryvora, and CB-23 escaped. Sion and the other members of Jade Squadron returned to the ''Colossus'' and celebrated their victory at [[Aunt Z's Tavern]].

==Biography==
===New Republic service===
{{Quote|Um, Kaz and I flew together back in the New Republic Navy.|Hugh Sion introduces Kazuda Xiono to Norath Kev|audio=HughSion1-RebuildingTheResistance.flac|<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />}}
[[File:HughSion-TheRecruitPart1.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Hugh Sion piloted a T-85 X-wing for the New Republic Starfighter Corps.]]
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="S1Date">{{ResistanceDate|1}}</ref> during the [[Cold War]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[New Republic]] and its allies, the [[human]] Hugh Sion served as the [[New Republic pilot|pilot]] of a [[T-85 X-wing starfighter]] in the [[New Republic Defense Force]]'s [[New Republic Defense Fleet Starfighter Corps|Starfighter Corps]].<ref name="The Recruit" /> He,<ref name="Databank" /> along with [[Kazuda Xiono's team|fellow pilots]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and [[Mia Gabon]], was sent on a [[Mission to rendezvous with the Resistance|mission]] to rendezvous with [[Commander]] [[Poe Dameron]] of the [[Resistance]] to deliver intelligence.<ref name="The Recruit" />

However, after arriving at the rendezvous point, the three pilots were ambushed by [[Major]] [[Elrik Vonreg]] of the First Order, and Sion and Gabon were concerned that the mission would fail. Xiono ordered the two [[pilot]]s to flee into [[hyperspace]] while he covered them. Following Sion and Gabon's jump to hyperspace, Xiono's [[starfighter]] was struck by Vonreg, but the pilot was saved by Commander Dameron. Rather than returning to base, Xiono opted to join the Resistance,<ref name="The Recruit" /> causing Sion and Gabon to assume the worst.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

===Flying under Jade Squadron===
{{Quote|Hugh! Buddy! Oh, I can't believe it! You're a pilot for the Resistance now?"<br />"Yeah, sure am, if you can believe that.|Hugh Sion and Kazuda Xiono reunite aboard the ''Colossus''|audio=HughSion2-RebuildingTheResistance.flac|<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />}}
[[File:HughSionKazudaXiono-RebuildingTheResistance.jpg|thumb|300px|right|Sion and Xiono reunite aboard the ''Colossus''.]]
Sion himself later joined the Resistance during the [[First Order-Resistance War]], flying a [[T-70 X-wing starfighter]] for [[Jade Squadron]] under Commander [[Venisa Doza]]. Doza's husband, [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza]] of the ''[[Colossus]]'', allowed them to travel to the [[supertanker fuel depot]] for a [[Mission to Dantooine (Resistance)|mission]] to escort Resistance recruits off the [[Blockade of Dantooine|First Order-controlled]] [[planet]] [[Dantooine]]. Once aboard, Sion was reunited with Xiono when he spotted Xiono admiring the [[carbon scoring]] on his fighter. Sion introduced his former [[wingmate]] to fellow Jade Squadron member [[Norath Kev]], who proceeded to explain that the [[squadron]] had been searching [[the galaxy]] for allies to stand against the First Order with mixed results, and with several members lost.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

After Captain Doza agreed to allow the squadron to temporarily house the Resistance recruits on the ''Colossus'', Xiono and [[Torra Doza]], daughter of Venisa and Imanuel, volunteered to assist with the mission. Venisa then recruited [[ace]] pilot [[Hype Fazon]], who joined the squadron for a briefing in the [[Aces' Lounge]], taking Sion's seat as he left to express his annoyance with Fazon's personality to Xiono. Venisa conducted her briefing, explaining the mission objectives: sneak onto Dantooine, evacuate the Resistance recruits, and avoid detection by the First Order. The pilots then proceeded to their fighters and left the ''Colossus'' for Dantooine.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

===Mission to Dantooine===
{{Quote|You got a shadow, Kaz. I'm on it."<br />"Whoo! Thanks for watching my back, Hugh.|Hugh Sion saves Kazuda Xiono from pursuit by Tamara Ryvora|audio=HughSion3-RebuildingTheResistance.flac|<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />}}
[[File:SionSavesKaz-RebuildingTheResistance.png|thumb|300px|left|Sion saves Xiono from Ryvora.]]
Upon approach to Dantooine, Sion explained to the rest of Jade Squadron that Xiono had nearly been thrown out of the [[New Republic Military Academy]] a couple of times. Shortly after, the squadron was attacked by a [[scout]]ing party of [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter]]s. Commander Doza ordered their communications [[Jammer|jammed]], and Jade Squadron split into pairs. After defeating the entire scouting party, Venisa contacted the Resistance recruits on-planet, and the [[Resistance shuttle|transports]] launched.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

As the squadron was escorting the [[convoy]] through Dantooine's [[atmosphere]], the [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]]<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" /> ''[[Thunderer]]'',<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> which had been alerted to Resistance activity on the planet, arrived. As the First Order forces&mdash;including [[Tamara Ryvora]] and [[Jace Rucklin]],<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" /> both former residents of the ''Colossus''<ref name="No Escape 1">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 1}}</ref>&mdash;approached, Venisa ordered Sion and Xiono to flank the enemy while she hit them head on. During the dogfight, Ryvora trailed Xiono, but Sion was able to damage her fighter, causing her to lose Xiono. Rucklin managed to take out [[Shuttle two (Resistance)|one]] of the transports, but the remaining two escaped into hyperspace along with Jade Squadron. Upon returning to the ''Colossus'', Sion conversed with Fazon, the other Aces, and a group of recruits.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

===Escaping the First Order===
{{Quote|All right, team, we're going for their engines. Jade Squadron, focus ion bombs on the panels near their thrusters. If we get close enough, we might have a chance of taking them out.|Venisa Doza, to Sion and the rest of Jade Squadron|audio=VenisaLeadingJade-TheEscape.flac|<ref name="The Escape" />}}
[[File:JadeAceBarabeshLaunch-TheEscape.png|thumb|right|300px|Jade and Ace Squadrons launch to defend the ''Colossus'' from the ''Thunderer''.]]
Later that same year, the ''Colossus'' traveled to the [[Barabesh system]] while evading the First Order. Shortly after, Xiono and the [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Jarek Yeager]] attempted a [[Battle of Barabesh|rescue]] of Ryvora after she expressed wanting to leave the First Order and return to the ''Colossus''. The rescue attempt initially failed, however, and the trio was captured by the First Order's [[Agent]] [[Tierny]] and Commander [[Pyre]] and brought aboard the ''Thunderer'', which headed to the Barabesh system to destroy the ''Colossus''.<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Imanuel gathered the denizens of the supertanker, including Sion, in [[Aunt Z's Tavern]] and pled with them to fight the First Order. Upon watching a [[hologram]] of Xiono and Ryvora begging them to flee, Sion and the rest of the citizens of the ''Colossus'' were moved to fight back.<ref name="The Escape" />

After the ''Thunderer''&mdash;under the command of Tierny&mdash;arrived in the [[Star system|system]], Jade Squadron, along with the ''Colossus''{{'s}} own [[Ace Squadron]], launched to defend the tanker and attacked the ''Thunderer''{{'s}} [[engine]]s, focusing their [[ion bomb]]s on the panels adjacent to the [[Starship|ship's]] thrusters. After several ineffective runs, the [[astromech droid]] [[CB-23]] managed to deactivate the [[Star Destroyer]]'s [[Deflector shield|shields]] from inside the ship, allowing Jade and Ace Squadrons to inflict damage on the engines. After a final pass with their [[proton torpedo]]s, the fighters destroyed the engines, causing a chain reaction throughout the ''Thunderer'' and killing Tierny and Pyre shortly after Xiono, Yeager, Ryvora, and CB-23 escaped aboard an [[Unidentified AAL-1971/9.1 Troop Transport|AAL-1971/9.1 Troop Transport]]. Sion and the other pilots rejoined with Kaz and the rest of the newly dubbed [[Team Colossus|Team ''Colossus'']] at [[Z'Vk'Thkrkza|Aunt Z's]] Tavern, celebrating their victory over the First Order.<ref name="The Escape" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Uh, what about you? I mean, last I saw, you were facing off against the red TIE, and...we assumed the worst.|Hugh Sion, to Kazuda Xiono|audio=HughSion4-RebuildingTheResistance.flac|<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />}}
[[File:TeamColossus-TheEscape.png|thumb|left|300px|Sion and the rest of Team ''Colossus'' celebrate their victory over the First Order.]]
Sion was a [[Gender|male]]<ref name="Bucket's List" /> human with [[Color|blue]] [[eye]]s, light skin, and brown [[hair]]. When Xiono failed to return to base after their mission to rendezvous with Dameron, Sion assumed the worst had happened, expressing concern in his voice when explaining his and Gabon's feelings about their friend's disappearance. Upon seeing Xiono admiring his beaten-up starfighter, the pilot jokingly scolded his friend for drooling on his ship. Sion expressed sorrow when explaining to Xiono that there were only a few members of Jade Squadron remaining. He also expressed annoyance when Fazon joined Jade Squadron in the Aces' Lounge and passively boasted about his piloting skills. During the flight to Dantooine, the pilot told the rest of the squadron Xiono had nearly been expelled from the Academy multiple times, finding humor in the story.<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" /> After the defeat of the ''Thunderer'', Sion celebrated with the rest of Team ''Colossus''.<ref name="The Escape" />

==Skills and abilities==
Sion was capable of piloting both T-85 and T-70 X-wing starfighters as a member of the New Republic Starfighter Corps and the Resistance, respectively.<ref name="The Recruit" /><ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Hey! No drooling on my ship.|Hugh Sion, to Kazuda Xiono in jest|audio=HughSion5-RebuildingTheResistance.flac|<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />}}
Sion flew a blue New Republic T-85 X-wing starfighter on his mission to rendezvous with Commander Dameron. While flying the X-wing, he wore a blue New Republic [[flight suit]] with the [[Sigil of the New Republic]] on the left shoulder and a [[helmet]] with a [[polarizing visor]] attached via a [[breathing tube]].<ref name="The Recruit" /> As a pilot of Jade Squadron, Sion flew a gray Resistance T-70 X-wing starfighter with blue markings that was scarred with carbon scoring, and he wore an orange Resistance flight suit with a white helmet with green markings and a green [[Rebel Alliance starbird]]; black [[glove]]s, shoes, and [[belt]]; and a white [[flak vest]].<ref name="Rebuilding the Resistance" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:SamVoicingHugh-RebuildingtheResistanceBucketsList.png|thumb|right|300px|Sam Witwer voiced Hugh Sion.]]
Hugh Sion first appeared in "[[The Recruit]]," the first part of the first episode of [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|Season One]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'',<ref name="The Recruit" /> which originally aired on [[October 7]], [[2018]].<ref name="Air date">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> The pilot was voiced by veteran ''[[Star Wars]]'' actor [[Sam Witwer]].<ref name="Bucket's List" /> On [[September 5]], 2018, artist [[Stephan A. Carey]] created concept art of Sion for "[[Rebuilding the Resistance]],"<ref name="Concept art">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-resistance/rebuilding-the-resistance-episode-guide|text="Rebuilding the Resistance" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Resistance}} {{C|Concept Art Gallery slide 9}}</ref> the seventeenth episode of the series' second season, which aired on [[January 19]], [[2020]].<ref name="Air date" />

